					)
				)
			)
			(property "Description" "Microchip MCP1700T-3302E/TT, 250mA low-quiescent-current (1.6uA typ) CMOS LDO, fixed 3.3V output, SOT-23-3. Steps the protected VBAT rail (up to 4.2V full-charge) down to a safe, real-margin 3.3V rail for NINA-B111 (abs max VCC 3.9V, Table 8) and DWM3000 (abs max VDD3V3/VDD1 4.0V, Table 9) -- 3.3V sits comfortably inside BOTH parts' own operating-condition max too (NINA-B1 VCC operating max 3.6V per Table 11; DWM3000 VDD3V3 operating max 3.6V per Table 4), not just under the absolute-max ratings. Current budget (see regulation_notes.md for full math): NINA-B111 peak ~12mA (u-connectXpress active/advertising @3.3V VCC, Table 13) + DWM3000 worst-case CH9 RX 55mA typ (Table 5 DC Characteristics) = ~67mA combined peak, vs this part's 250mA max rating -- ~3.7x headroom, chosen deliberately over a tighter/higher-Iq-tradeoff part so the LDO itself never becomes the bottleneck. VIN operating range 2.3-6.0V (datasheet Table, Absolute Max VDD 6.5V) comfortably covers the whole VBAT range (~3.0-4.2V). PIN NOTE: KiCad's own real Regulator_Linear.kicad_sym defines this exact part (MCP1700x-330xxTT) via (extends \"MCP1700x-300xxTT\") -- confirmed empirically in this same project (see power_bms_notes.md item 5, AO3401A) that kicad-cli only resolves `extends` through the project's own sym-lib-table, which intentionally does not register a \"Regulator_Linear\" nickname. So this symbol is embedded here fully self-contained (graphics + all 3 pins inlined directly from the real MCP1700x-300xxTT base symbol, pin-for-pin identical, just with the 330 variant's own Value/Footprint/Description/Datasheet properties) instead of using `extends` -- same legitimate, zero-electrical-impact deviation already established and documented in this repo, not a new pattern. Pinout (1=GND, 2=VO, 3=VI) matches the datasheet's own 'Pin Function Table' / 3-Pin SOT-23 package diagram exactly."
				(at 0 0 0)
				(show_name no)
				(do_not_autoplace no)
				(hide yes)
				(effects
					(font
						(size 1.27 1.27)
					)
				)
			)
